From 28db3ae98021620c44d4687e6fad612adee808ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanju Abraham <s.abraham@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 00:25:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat(governance): populate users in-memory cache on
 reload

- Adds `GetUsers(ctx) ([]TableUser, error)` to ConfigStore interface +
  RDB impl (preloads Team/Budgets/RateLimit, ordered by created_at).
- Adds `Users []TableUser` to GovernanceConfig and threads it through
  the GovernanceConfig builder (GetGovernanceConfig in rdb.go).
- Adds `users sync.Map` to LocalGovernanceStore alongside teams/customers.
- Adds users param to rebuildInMemoryStructures; populates gs.users
  keyed by user.ID.
- Both reload paths (loadFromDatabase + loadFromConfigMemory) now
  fetch / pass users through to rebuildInMemoryStructures.

Subsequent patches implement the governance enforcement (CheckUserBudget,
CheckUserRateLimit) and resolver wire-up (VK-implies-user via FK)
against this populated cache.
---
 framework/configstore/clientconfig.go |  1 +
 framework/configstore/rdb.go          | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 framework/configstore/store.go        |  1 +
 plugins/governance/store.go           | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 4 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

